燃烧的玉米地和跳动的205号车不见了，
Out went the burning cornfields
and the jumping 205s,

901
00:48:59,380 --> 00:49:01,820
随之而来的是这玩意儿……
and in came tosh like this...

902
00:49:03,300 --> 00:49:05,930
买辆车，四个轮子和几把座椅
Buy a car, four wheels and some seats

903
00:49:05,980 --> 00:49:07,410
每月仅需99英镑
for just £99 a month

904
00:49:07,460 --> 00:49:10,610
再送1000镑返现，加上另外2000镑返现。
with £1,000 cashback plus
another £2,000 cashback.

905
00:49:10,660 --> 00:49:13,250
轻松融资，还免费——对，免费——
Easy finance and a free - yes, free -

906
00:49:13,300 --> 00:49:15,440
锁定的油箱盖！
locking petrol filler cap!

907
00:49:16,660 --> 00:49:19,010
年利率 29.4%。受条款和条件约束。
APR 29.4%. Subject to
terms and conditions.

908
00:49:19,060 --> 00:49:21,050
想拥有车子，你得能签下你的名字。
You must be able to sign
your name to have a car.

909
00:49:21,100 --> 00:49:25,000
如果不按时还款，你的膝盖可能会受伤。
Your knees may be at risk if
you do not keep up repayments.

910
00:49:26,340 --> 00:49:28,770
效果立竿见影。
The results were immediate.

911
00:49:28,820 --> 00:49:31,250
销量直线上升。
Sales went through the roof.

912
00:49:31,300 --> 00:49:35,250
标致可能擅长造结实和运动型的车，
Peugeot may have been good at making
sturdy cars and sporty cars,

913
00:49:35,300 --> 00:49:41,370
但他们显然在造烂车方面简直是天才。
but it seemed they were absolutely
brilliant at making terrible cars.

914
00:49:41,420 --> 00:49:43,810
是啊。想看看有多厉害，
Yes. And to find out
just how brilliant,

915
00:49:43,860 --> 00:49:45,970
我和杰里米要来一次实验。
Jeremy and I are going
to do an experiment.

916
00:49:46,020 --> 00:49:49,930
他买了这辆有点儿被火烤过的307 CC。
He has bought this mildly
fire-damaged 307 CC.

917
00:49:49,980 --> 00:49:51,890
你可以看到刚才火灾的痕迹就在这儿。
You can see where the
fire was just here.

918
00:49:51,940 --> 00:49:53,890
现在已经熄了，没事。
It's out now, so that's OK.

919
00:49:53,940 --> 00:49:55,050
好啊。是的。
Good. Yes.

920
00:49:55,100 --> 00:49:58,930
而我买了这辆极其沉闷的407。
And I have bought this
utterly dreary 407.

921
00:49:58,980 --> 00:50:01,330
好了，现在我们要来试试这些车。
And now, we're going to test them

922
00:50:01,380 --> 00:50:04,980
好像我们根本不关心汽车一样。
as if we're not interested
in cars at all.

923
00:50:08,460 --> 00:50:11,090
在这些糟糕的车里，
In these horrible cars,
it didn't take us long

924
00:50:11,140 --> 00:50:14,810
我们很快就掌握了现代标致车手的感觉。
to get the hang of being
modern Peugeot drivers.

925
00:50:21,020 --> 00:50:22,360
疯子！
Maniac!

926
00:50:24,860 --> 00:50:27,300
然后……转向……
And...turn...

927
00:50:31,260 --> 00:50:36,650
到底是怎么回事，那些《Top Gear》里的蠢货为什么要吐槽标致？
Why oh why do those idiots
on Top Gear criticise Peugeot?

928
00:50:36,700 --> 00:50:39,810
你看，六速变速箱。
I mean, look, six-speed gear box.

929
00:50:39,860 --> 00:50:41,570
这玩意儿简直太棒了——
This is particularly brilliant -

930
00:50:41,620 --> 00:50:44,610
这里有灯开关，关着，然后这里，
you've got your light switch
here, off, and then here,

931
00:50:44,660 --> 00:50:46,330
尤其是关着的那个。
especially off.

932
00:50:50,820 --> 00:50:55,690
所以两转……两转半，再换档……
So two... two-and-a-half
revs, another gear...

933
00:50:57,660 --> 00:51:00,200
哦不，你应该踩……
Oh, no, you're supposed to press...

934
00:51:02,300 --> 00:51:03,770
就这么简单。
That's it.

935
00:51:07,100 --> 00:51:09,980
结果，詹姆斯马上撞车了。
Soon, James had an accident.

936
00:51:16,340 --> 00:51:18,010
该死，真是气死我。
Damn and blast.

937
00:51:18,740 --> 00:51:20,140
哎呀，天呐。
Oh, dear.

938
00:51:20,980 --> 00:51:22,980
哎呀，呀呀呀……
Oh, dear, dear, dear...

939
00:51:32,060 --> 00:51:35,130
~ 你又撞了？
~ 是啊。
~ You crashed again?
~ Yeah.

940
00:51:35,180 --> 00:51:37,290
你今天早上不是在这个弯上撞过吗？
Didn't you crash on this
corner this morning?

941
00:51:37,340 --> 00:51:39,690
是啊，我到现在都还没绕过去一次。
Yeah. I haven't got
round it once yet.

942
00:51:39,740 --> 00:51:42,610
这太刁钻了，我不知道他们为什么要在这里拐弯……
It is tricky. I don't know
why they put corners on...

943
00:51:42,660 --> 00:51:44,090
我真想问，为什么要这么设计？
I mean, why would you?

944
00:51:44,140 --> 00:51:45,890
好吧，我当时开得挺快的。
Well, I was going quite fast.

945
00:51:45,940 --> 00:51:47,010
我还在三挡。
I was in third.

946
00:51:47,060 --> 00:51:48,260
啊！
Oh!

947
00:51:49,420 --> 00:51:52,330
就在詹姆斯的车被拖出沟外的时候，
While James's car was being
towed out of the ditch,

948
00:51:52,380 --> 00:51:54,530
我趁机展示了一下
I took the opportunity to demonstrate

949
00:51:54,580 --> 00:51:57,820
我车上又一个令人惊叹的标配功能。
yet another incredible standard
feature on my car.

950
00:51:58,900 --> 00:52:00,930
如果你想把副驾驶的窗户降下来，
If you want to lower
the passenger window,

951
00:52:00,980 --> 00:52:04,380
只要在司机侧门上的开关一按就行。
you can do that from a switch
on the driver's door.

952
00:52:05,340 --> 00:52:09,410
但要把它升回去……你根本做不到。
But if you want to get it
back up again... you can't.

953
00:52:09,460 --> 00:52:13,690
所以只能从另一侧去操作，行吧，
So, you have to go round
to the other side, OK,

954
00:52:13,740 --> 00:52:16,330
然后按这里的按钮。
and use the button here.

955
00:52:16,380 --> 00:52:23,170
不过这么一来，你的胳膊会卡在这缝里。
But, if you do that, you're going
to trap your arm in this gap here.

956
00:52:23,220 --> 00:52:26,290
标致想的真周到，行吧？显然，这扇门根本打不开。
Now, Peugeot's thought of that, OK?
Obviously, you can't open this door.

957
00:52:26,340 --> 00:52:28,610
没有门锁，这都是所谓的安全考虑。
There's no door lock, that's
for security reasons.

958
00:52:28,660 --> 00:52:34,090
于是你得绕回来——这玩意儿真是太神奇了——
So you pop back round here
- and this is incredible -

959
00:52:34,140 --> 00:52:37,610
只要拉一下这个开关，行吧？
simply pull this switch, OK?

960
00:52:37,660 --> 00:52:39,730
窗户全都降下来了。
Windows ALL go down now.

961
00:52:40,980 --> 00:52:43,500
车顶掉下来，现在……
The roof detaches, and now...

962
00:52:44,900 --> 00:52:48,850
看看，我居然能把车窗掀起来
Now look - I can lift the window

963
00:52:48,900 --> 00:52:52,570
而且手一点儿都不被卡住。
without getting my arm trapped.

964
00:52:52,620 --> 00:52:55,220
看见了没？太妙了。
Can you see? Brilliant.

965
00:52:58,860 --> 00:53:00,690
詹姆斯的车子已经脱离沟渠，
With James's car out of the ditch,

966
00:53:00,740 --> 00:53:04,620
我们放松下来，调到标致广播。
we relaxed by tuning
in to Radio Peugeot.

967
00:53:06,140 --> 00:53:08,490
Jeremy Vine，BBC 2台。
Jeremy Vine, BBC Radio 2.

968
00:53:08,540 --> 00:53:10,890
“英国满了吗？”我们就是这么开场的。
"Is Britain full?" is
how we started this.

969
00:53:10,940 --> 00:53:13,490
伯克郡沃菲尔的Alison发来短信说，
Alison in Warfield in
Berkshire texts and says,

970
00:53:13,540 --> 00:53:15,610
“我在Waitrose根本找不到停车位。”
"I can't park at Waitrose.

971
00:53:15,660 --> 00:53:17,770
“所以，是的，我们太满了。”
"So, yes, we are too full."

972
00:53:17,820 --> 00:53:19,420
好来电。
Good caller.

973
00:53:23,340 --> 00:53:26,250
他真是太客气了，刚刚轻轻推了我一下
That's very nice of him. He just
gave me a little push there

974
00:53:26,300 --> 00:53:28,840
让我知道他要从我身边经过。
to let me know he was coming past.

975
00:53:30,900 --> 00:53:32,570
拐弯！拐弯！
Corner! Corner!

976
00:53:45,380 --> 00:53:47,450
搞定，我转弯成功。
I've done it. I'm round.

977
00:53:49,940 --> 00:53:53,050
尽管标致广播的柔和旋律……
Despite the soothing tones
of Radio Peugeot...

978
00:53:53,100 --> 00:53:56,090
你们觉得这水是不是全英最难喝的？
Do you think you may have the
worst-tasting water in Britain?

979
00:53:56,140 --> 00:53:57,970
要是这样，赶紧打给我们——0500 288 291…
Do call us if so - 0500 288 291...

980
00:53:58,020 --> 00:54:00,490
……我们觉得这段旅程压力山大
.. we found the journey
very stressful

981
00:54:00,540 --> 00:54:03,140
全怪那些乱七八糟的路标……
thanks to badly placed road signs...

982
00:54:06,060 --> 00:54:08,060
还有那些拥挤的十字路口。
.. and busy junctions.

983
00:54:09,300 --> 00:54:10,640
疯子。
Maniac.

984
00:54:11,460 --> 00:54:12,800
疯子。
Maniac.

985
00:54:13,500 --> 00:54:14,970
疯子。
Maniac.

986
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:16,530
流氓。
Yobbo.

987
00:54:16,580 --> 00:54:17,810
疯子。
Maniac.

988
00:54:17,860 --> 00:54:20,860
疯子……呃等下，我好像看到机会了。
Mani... oh, hold on, I think
there's a chance here.

989
00:54:23,540 --> 00:54:26,010
哎呀……该死！
Ohhh... damn it!

990
00:54:26,060 --> 00:54:28,410
你们这儿来了个Johnny Foreigner，
You've got Johnny Foreigner
coming over here,

991
00:54:28,460 --> 00:54:30,600
他们连分钱都不付……
they don't pay a penny...

992
00:54:35,060 --> 00:54:38,060
该死的议会还不修那该死的路。
Bloody council not mending
the bloody roads.

993
00:54:42,780 --> 00:54:45,250
詹姆斯，前面有个弯，一个弯。
James, there's a corner
coming up, a corner.

994
00:54:45,300 --> 00:54:48,380
路标上写着“弯”，这次小心点，好吗？
There's a sign saying, "corner".
Do take care this time, OK?

995
00:54:52,580 --> 00:54:55,730
说实话，我根本没注意到詹姆斯最新的事故
To be honest, I didn't notice
James's latest accident

996
00:54:55,780 --> 00:55:00,130
因为我刚在我这辆超棒的车里发现了新功能。
because I'd found yet another
feature in my amazing car.

997
00:55:00,180 --> 00:55:04,650
如果我在这里按下这个能升温的按钮，
If I push this button here that
increases the temperature,

998
00:55:04,700 --> 00:55:08,050
再稍微踩一下……
and then hold it down
for a little while...

999
00:55:08,100 --> 00:55:10,610
好了，搞定。
There we go.

1000
00:55:10,660 --> 00:55:14,650
太棒了，太棒了。嗯——，烟雾！
Lovely, lovely. Mm-mm, smoke!

1001
00:55:14,700 --> 00:55:17,370
显然，你得先闷一闷气。
Obviously, there's a fair bit of
choking you have to go through,

1002
00:55:17,420 --> 00:55:19,940
但是，呃……看看这结果！
but, um... look at the result!

1003
00:55:21,460 --> 00:55:25,690
人们想要……真正的火焰在家里燃起。
People like a... a real
fire in their homes.

1004
00:55:25,740 --> 00:55:27,740
我车里就有一把。
I've got one in my car.

1005
00:55:28,940 --> 00:55:31,170
幸好这车有个烟囱。
It's a good job this
car has a chimney.

1006
00:55:31,220 --> 00:55:34,220
这显然是个超棒的设计。
Obviously, that's a very
good design feature.

1007
00:55:35,940 --> 00:55:37,770
我再和詹姆斯碰面时，
When I met up with James again,

1008
00:55:37,820 --> 00:55:41,610
地点正是标致司机的噩梦——
it was at the Peugeot driver's
worst nightmare -

1009
00:55:41,660 --> 00:55:43,980
双层小环岛。
a double mini-roundabout.

1010
00:55:46,860 --> 00:55:48,130
现在……
Now...

1011
00:55:55,140 --> 00:55:57,540
天啊。好，这一切都清楚了……
Dear God. Right, that's clear...

1012
00:56:13,780 --> 00:56:15,380
我真不知道。
I don't know.

1013
00:56:19,140 --> 00:56:20,500
这……
It's...

1014
00:56:33,820 --> 00:56:35,160
疯子！
Maniac!

1015
00:56:40,220 --> 00:56:44,100
天呐——再也别出现双层小环岛了，拜托。
Oh, God - no more double
mini-roundabouts ever, please.

1016
00:56:46,100 --> 00:56:48,170
经历了如此惊心动魄的折磨后，
After such a terrifying ordeal,

1017
00:56:48,220 --> 00:56:51,530
我们得来杯热甜茶安抚神经，
we needed hot sweet tea
to calm our nerves,

1018
00:56:51,580 --> 00:56:54,220
于是直奔附近的园艺中心。
so we went to a nearby garden centre.

1019
00:56:55,380 --> 00:56:58,610
Will Hull 发邮件说：“我建议我们把救济院重新引进来。”
Will Hull e-mails, "I suggest
we bring back workhouses.

1020
00:56:58,660 --> 00:57:00,810
“这会阻止人们利用国家”
"That would deter people
exploiting the state

1021
00:57:00,860 --> 00:57:04,010
~ “并且让他们随心所欲生孩子。” ~ 差不多就算是个空间了。
~ "and having as many children as they want."
~ A space there, nearly.

1022
00:57:04,060 --> 00:57:05,460
入口？
Entrance?

1023
00:57:14,980 --> 00:57:17,320
我得正面进去。
I'll have to come in forwards.

1024
00:57:33,260 --> 00:57:36,020
来杯茶。哦……完美。
A cup of tea. Ooh... perfect.

1025
00:57:48,980 --> 00:57:51,010
~ 看到这个了吗，詹姆斯？ ~ 什么？
~ Have you seen this, James?
~ What?

1026
00:57:51,060 --> 00:57:55,250
~ 胡萝卜能防癌。 ~ 真的吗？ ~ 是啊。
~ Carrots stop you getting cancer.
~ Really?
~ Yeah.

1027
00:57:55,300 --> 00:57:57,090
但《邮报》说是番……番茄。
But The Mail said it
was toma... tomatoes.

1028
00:57:57,140 --> 00:58:00,010
还是说番茄会致癌？
Or was it tomatoes give you cancer?

1029
00:58:00,060 --> 00:58:03,970
我还以为黛安娜会让你得癌症。还是说房价？
I thought Diana gave you cancer.
Or was it house prices?

1030
00:58:04,020 --> 00:58:06,450
不，移民才把房价…
No, immigrants do house pr...

1031
00:58:06,500 --> 00:58:08,370
哦，我搞糊涂了。
Oh, I get confused.

1032
00:58:08,420 --> 00:58:12,060
下午茶结束，我们继续上路。
'Afternoon tea over, we
got back on the road.'

1033
00:58:19,740 --> 00:58:21,080
疯子！
Maniac!

1034
00:58:23,780 --> 00:58:26,010
忙碌一天后，我们正要回家，
After a busy day, we
were heading home,

1035
00:58:26,060 --> 00:58:28,450
为了到达目的地，我们在车上装了
and to get there,
we'd fitted our cars

1036
00:58:28,500 --> 00:58:32,210
所谓的“卫星导航”。
with something called
"satellite navigation".

1037
00:58:32,260 --> 00:58:35,890
这玩意儿太神奇了。是我孩子送的礼物。
Incredible device. It was
a present from my children.

1038
00:58:35,940 --> 00:58:41,290
它知道我在地球上的位置，然后能指引我回家。
It knows where I am on the planet
and then it can get me to my house.

1039
00:58:41,340 --> 00:58:43,740
我只需要乖乖听它指示。
All I have to do is as I'm told.

1040
00:58:44,460 --> 00:58:48,940
于是我左拐……对的……
So I go left here... yes...

1041
00:58:50,540 --> 00:58:54,380
好，我按照电图指示，往右走。
Right, according to the
electric map, I go right.

1042
00:58:56,660 --> 00:58:58,260
这个啊，嗯……
This is, um...

1043
00:58:59,620 --> 00:59:01,890
……长得太荒废了，市政局真该出点手。
.. overgrown - the council
should really do something

1044
00:59:01,940 --> 00:59:03,880
关于这条路。
about this road here.

1045
00:59:05,100 --> 00:59:07,410
怪不得吧？这事儿你经常听说。
It's weird, isn't it? You
hear stories all the time

1046
00:59:07,460 --> 00:59:11,370
关于那些蠢货，"哦，我在用卫星导航呢"
about idiots who, "Oh, I was following
the satellite navigation

1047
00:59:11,420 --> 00:59:13,690
"结果车子直接掉悬崖，掉进运河"
"and I drove off a cliff
or into a canal",

1048
00:59:13,740 --> 00:59:16,080
你只能想，"真是个脑残！"
and you think, "What a moron!"

1049
00:59:20,540 --> 00:59:24,100
一定是所谓的捷径，真是太聪明了。
Must be a shortcut. Bloody clever.

1050
00:59:28,860 --> 00:59:32,730
结果我们到了，回家甜蜜蜜！
And here we are. Home sweet home!

1051
00:59:32,780 --> 00:59:35,060
啊，爽啊！
Ah, joy!

1052
00:59:37,860 --> 00:59:40,370
于是我们来了——标致。
So, there we are - Peugeot.

1053
00:59:40,420 --> 00:59:43,450
他们过去很擅长造坚固的车。
They were brilliant
at making strong cars.

1054
00:59:43,500 --> 00:59:45,730
也很擅长造运动型车，
They were brilliant
at making sporty cars,

1055
00:59:45,780 --> 00:59:47,210
但过去十年里，
and for the last decade,

1056
00:59:47,260 --> 00:59:51,010
他们却擅长造烂车。
they have been brilliant
at making terrible cars.

1057
00:59:51,060 --> 00:59:57,010
这真是为全世界不完美司机量身定做的完美座驾。
This really is THE perfect car
for the world's imperfect drivers.

1058
00:59:57,060 --> 00:59:59,890
“要让人不超速，最简单的方法就是给他们判监狱”。
"The simple way to stop speeding
is to hand a jail sentence

1059
00:59:59,940 --> 01:00:02,130
“给任何被抓到超速的人”。
"to anyone who's caught
breaking the speed limit,

1060
01:00:02,180 --> 01:00:04,170
“这样就能解决问题”。
"and that will sort the problem."

1061
01:00:04,220 --> 01:00:06,360
肯特郡拉姆斯盖特的珍妮……
Jenny in Ramsgate, Kent...

1062
01:00:09,340 --> 01:00:10,650
但问题来了。
But here's the worry.

1063
01:00:10,700 --> 01:00:14,090
很快，标致就又该改主意了
Soon, it will be time for Peugeot
to change its mind again

1064
01:00:14,140 --> 01:00:15,810
再想出点新玩意儿。
and think of something new.

1065
01:00:15,860 --> 01:00:17,730
谁知道会是什么玩意儿。
And who knows what that'll be.

1066
01:00:17,780 --> 01:00:20,180
要是标致，可能会是…
Knowing Peugeot, it could be...

1067
01:00:20,380 --> 01:00:22,380
一种惰性气体。
.. a type of inert gas.

1068
01:00:23,140 --> 01:00:26,370
标致九人节奏蓝调乐队。
The Peugeot nine-piece
Rhythm and Blues band.

1069
01:00:26,420 --> 01:00:29,290
只有时间会告诉我们。
Only time will tell.

1070
01:00:41,100 --> 01:00:42,330
真的？
Really?

1071
01:00:42,380 --> 01:00:44,730
有史以来Top Gear最糟的事，窒息——
Worst thing ever on Top
Gear, the choking -

1072
01:00:44,780 --> 01:00:48,010
我从来，从未遇到更烂的
I've never, never ever
had anything worse

1073
01:00:48,060 --> 01:00:50,290
比被烧车闷死更糟的。
than being choked to
death in a car on fire.

1074
01:00:50,340 --> 01:00:52,330
~ 等一下。
~ 什么？
~ 稍等会儿。
~ Hang on.
~ What?
~ Hang on a minute.

1075
01:00:52,380 --> 01:00:56,490
你们俩是说标致已经花了十年
Are you two saying that Peugeot
have spent ten years

1076
01:00:56,540 --> 01:00:58,970
故意在造烂车？
deliberately making terrible cars?

1077
01:00:59,020 --> 01:01:03,250
~ 嗯。
~ 嗯，是啊——烂车不可能偶然一直这么烂。
~ Mm.
~ Well, yeah - you can't make cars
that consistently bad by accident.

1078
01:01:03,300 --> 01:01:05,290
不对，想想吧，哈蒙德，想想。
No, think about it, Hammond,
think about it.

1079
01:01:05,340 --> 01:01:07,130
造车的意义何在
What is the point of making a car

1080
01:01:07,180 --> 01:01:09,330
配上复杂的刹车和昂贵的悬挂
with complicated brakes
and expensive suspension

1081
01:01:09,380 --> 01:01:11,170
如果你只是想把它卖给某个人
if you're just going
to sell it to someone

1082
01:01:11,220 --> 01:01:13,570
只想要杰里米·瓦恩还有省心的贷款？
who only wants Jeremy
Vine and easy finance?

1083
01:01:13,620 --> 01:01:15,930
没错——你们把车造得尽可能便宜
Exactly - you make cars
as cheaply as possible

1084
01:01:15,980 --> 01:01:17,890
然后卖给根本看不出区别的买家。
and then sell them to
people who won't notice.

1085
01:01:17,940 --> 01:01:20,890
我的意思是，换个角度想，好吗？就算我们现在说着，
I mean, think of it this way,
OK? Right now, even as we speak,

1086
01:01:20,940 --> 01:01:24,970
英国有九百万人对汽车毫无兴趣，
nine million people in Britain
are so uninterested in cars,

1087
01:01:25,020 --> 01:01:27,330
他们都在看那边的《助产士》节目。
they're watching that Midwife
thing on the other side.

1088
01:01:27,380 --> 01:01:29,890
你居然说他们全是标致车主？
And you're saying they're
all Peugeot drivers?

1089
01:01:29,940 --> 01:01:33,730
是啊，我就是这么说，而且他们会伤心到爆
Yes, I am, and they're all going
to be absolutely heartbroken

1090
01:01:33,780 --> 01:01:36,180
因为标致要开始造牛了。
when Peugeot starts making cows.

1091
01:01:37,260 --> 01:01:39,010
说到这爆炸性消息，节目该收尾了。
And on that bombshell,
it's time to end.

1092
01:01:39,060 --> 01:01:42,020
非常感谢收看，下周见，晚安！
Thank you so much for watching.
See you next week. Good night!

